1) Diff Btw GIT & Github

    GIT
    ====
    GIT is the version control software that runs locally on your machine. You dont need to register
    for an account. You dont need the internet to use it. You can use GIT without ever toughching Github.
                                                or
    👉 Git is a version control system used to track changes in files (mostly code) and help multiple developers
    work together on the same project.

    Github
    ======
    Github is a service that hosts Git repositories in the cloud and makes it easier to collaborate with other people.
    You do need to sign up for an account to use Github. It's an online place to share work that is done using Git.


2) Git repository
     " A Git repo is a storage location that contains project files along with their complete version history, allowing us
       to track changes and collaborate with others. "


3) Git status
     " git status is command used to check the current state of the repository. It shows which files are modified, staged 
        or untracked in the working directory."
